q-25135" :question/problem "Find $x$ such that ${log}_{4}(3x-2)=3.$" :question/worked-solution "To remove the logarithm, we exponentiate both sides of the equation. The base of the logarithm is $4,$ so we use this base for the exponentiation as well:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{4}(3x-2) & =3 \\\\ {4}^{{log}_{4}(3x-2)} & ={4}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since exponentiation is the inverse function of the logarithm, we get ${4}^{{log}_{4}(3x-2)}=3x-2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2 & ={4}^{3} \\\\ 3x-2 & =64 \\\\ 3x & =66 \\\\ x & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
